{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$h$ is a rational function.\n\nTo find the derivative of rational functions, we use **the quotient rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}\\right]\u0026=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)-u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{u'(x)v(x)-u(x)v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's differentiate!\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}h'(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{x^2+1}{2x^2-3x}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(2x^2-3x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^2+1)-(x^2+1)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(2x^2-3x)}{(2x^2-3x)^2}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{The quotient rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(2x^2-3x)(2x)-(x^2+1)(4x-3)}{(2x^2-3x)^2}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }(2x^2-3x)\\text{ \u0026 }(x^2+1)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{4x^3-6x^2-(4x^3-3x^2+4x-3)}{(2x^2-3x)^2}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Expand}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{4x^3-6x^2-4x^3+3x^2-4x+3}{(2x^2-3x)^2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{-3x^2-4x+3}{(2x^2-3x)^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $h'(x)=\\dfrac{-3x^2-4x+3}{(2x^2-3x)^2}$, or any other equivalent form.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $h(x)=\\dfrac{x^2+1}{2x^2-3x}$.\n\n$h'(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"\\frac{3-4x-3x^2}{\\left(2x^2-3x\\right)^2}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
